{"item":"Table::clear leaves a stack root","loc":"src/table.rs:417","sources":["P0012","P0013","P0014","P0015","P0016","P0017","P0018","P0117","P0141","P0194","P0195","P0196","P0197","P0198","P0199"],"reports":"ABCD","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"Lua 5.4 weak-value regression retains the cleared table after dropping its handle and collecting twice; untouched control is collected. Luau control passes. Non-Luau code lacks stack restoration."}
{"item":"Permissive Serde drops supported nulls","loc":"src/serde/de.rs:756","sources":["P0019","P0020","P0021","P0022","P0023","P0024","P0025","P0026","P0118","P0143","P0169","P0170","P0171","P0172","P0173","P0174","P0175"],"reports":"ABCD","status":"ran","severity":"high","noise_class":null,"note":"On Lua 5.4 and Luau, both conversion directions change {present:null,items:[null,1]} into {items:[1]}; default-option controls preserve it. The skip predicate includes null lightuserdata."}
{"item":"Table equality accepts longer slices and arrays","loc":"src/table.rs:914","sources":["P0027","P0028","P0029","P0030","P0031","P0032","P0033","P0121","P0145","P0188","P0189","P0190","P0191","P0192","P0193"],"reports":"ABCD","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"On Lua 5.4 and Luau, {1,2} equals [1,2,3] and an empty table equals [1]. Equal-length and shorter-slice controls behave correctly; the final return omits the length check."}
{"item":"Numeric sets fail their own round-trip conversion","loc":"src/conversion.rs:1078","sources":["P0034","P0035","P0036","P0037","P0038","P0039","P0040","P0119","P0182","P0183","P0184","P0185","P0186","P0187"],"reports":"ABD","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"HashSet<i32> and BTreeSet<i32> containing 1,2,3 fail with boolean-to-i32 errors on Lua 5.4 and Luau; string-set control passes. Membership tables are misclassified as sequences, also at line 1102."}
{"item":"Tuple variants omit the array metatable","loc":"src/serde/ser.rs:290","sources":["P0041","P0042","P0043","P0045","P0046","P0047","P0048"],"reports":"A","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"Default serialization of an empty tuple variant produces {Empty:{}} instead of {Empty:[]} on Lua 5.4 and Luau. Tuple-variant table creation bypasses the enabled array-metatable option."}
{"item":"Nil fields shift subsequent tuple-variant fields","loc":"src/serde/ser.rs:456","sources":["P0041","P0042","P0043","P0045","P0046","P0047","P0048","P0144"],"reports":"AC","status":"ran","severity":"high","noise_class":null,"note":"With serialize_none_to_null(false), Items(None,7) stores 7 at index 1 on Lua 5.4 and Luau; the ordinary-tuple control keeps it at index 2. raw_push recomputes the insertion index after nil."}
{"item":"Failed Luau vector-to-array conversion omits destructors","loc":"src/conversion.rs:960","sources":["P0049","P0050","P0051","P0052","P0053","P0054","P0055"],"reports":"A","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"A custom conversion accepts component 1 and rejects component 2: the destructor count is zero for a vector, one for the table control. MaybeUninit elements have no cleanup guard on early return."}
{"item":"Luau buffer relative seeks overflow before validation","loc":"src/buffer.rs:136","sources":["P0056","P0057","P0058","P0059","P0060","P0061","P0062","P0124","P0149","P0206","P0207","P0208","P0209","P0210","P0211"],"reports":"ABCD","status":"ran","severity":"low","noise_class":null,"note":"Debug tests panic on End(i64::MAX) and on Current(i64::MAX) from position 1 in a three-byte buffer. Ordinary invalid-seek control returns Err; release behavior was not tested."}
{"item":"Documentation links to disabled async APIs","loc":"src/lib.rs:42","sources":["P0063","P0064","P0065","P0066","P0067","P0068","P0069","P0111","P0212","P0213","P0214","P0215","P0216","P0217","P0254"],"reports":"AD","status":"not-defect","severity":null,"noise_class":"skill-requested-hygiene","note":"Strict baseline rustdoc fails on three async links at lines 42-44; enabling async removes those diagnostics. This is documentation/build hygiene."}
{"item":"Documentation cannot resolve the sandbox link","loc":"src/thread.rs:447","sources":["P0063","P0064","P0065","P0066","P0067","P0068","P0069","P0111","P0125","P0152","P0154","P0212","P0213","P0214","P0215","P0216","P0217","P0254","P0255","P0256"],"reports":"ABCD","status":"not-defect","severity":null,"noise_class":"skill-requested-hygiene","note":"Normal expanded-feature docs warn that Lua is not in scope for Lua::sandbox; -D warnings turns it into an error. This is a broken documentation reference."}
{"item":"Documentation Debug link is ambiguous","loc":"src/state.rs:880","sources":["P0063","P0064","P0065","P0066","P0067","P0068","P0069","P0111","P0125","P0152","P0154","P0212","P0213","P0214","P0215","P0216","P0217","P0254","P0255","P0256"],"reports":"ABCD","status":"not-defect","severity":null,"noise_class":"skill-requested-hygiene","note":"Normal docs warn that Debug names both a struct and derive macro; strict docs fail. Qualifying the link is documentation/build hygiene."}
{"item":"Path lookup rejects the minimum integer key","loc":"src/util/path.rs:81","sources":["P0071","P0072","P0073","P0074","P0075","P0076","P0077","P0151","P0225","P0226","P0227","P0228","P0229","P0230"],"reports":"ACD","status":"ran","severity":"low","noise_class":null,"note":"Lua 5.4 accepts the i64::MIN table key, but its bracket path returns integer overflow; adjacent-minimum and maximum controls pass. Positive signed accumulation overflows before negation."}
{"item":"Strict Clippy rejects redundant pointer casts on aarch64","loc":"src/conversion.rs:534","sources":["P0078","P0079","P0080","P0081","P0082","P0083","P0084","P0111","P0231","P0232","P0233","P0234","P0235","P0254"],"reports":"AD","status":"not-defect","severity":null,"noise_class":"skill-requested-hygiene","note":"Reproduced four unnecessary_cast diagnostics: conversion.rs:534/667, string.rs:133, util/mod.rs:279. Here c_char is u8; these casts do not change runtime behavior."}
{"item":"Strict Clippy rejects a redundant formatting borrow","loc":"src/error.rs:300","sources":["P0078","P0079","P0080","P0081","P0082","P0083","P0084","P0111","P0231","P0232","P0233","P0234","P0235","P0254"],"reports":"AD","status":"not-defect","severity":null,"noise_class":"skill-requested-hygiene","note":"Reproduced useless_borrows_in_formatting under -D warnings. The extra reference has no behavioral consequence."}
{"item":"Public documentation omits items and error sections","loc":"src/traits.rs:17","sources":["P0085","P0086","P0087","P0088","P0089","P0090","P0093","P0236","P0237","P0238","P0239"],"reports":"AD","status":"not-defect","severity":null,"noise_class":"skill-requested-hygiene","note":"Independent advisory Clippy reproduces 22 missing_docs, 116 missing_errors_doc and one missing_panics_doc diagnostics. Representative source omissions are documentation housekeeping."}
{"item":"Function::bind allegedly drops a trailing nil","loc":"src/function.rs:207","sources":["P0091"],"reports":"A","status":"refuted","severity":null,"noise_class":null,"note":"Regression returns all five arguments (11,nil,33,nil,44), with select count 5, on Lua 5.4 and Luau. The saved explicit upvalue count preserves trailing nils."}
{"item":"Serde allegedly rejects shared acyclic child tables","loc":"src/serde/de.rs:745","sources":["P0092"],"reports":"A","status":"refuted","severity":null,"noise_class":null,"note":"Default deserialization of two fields sharing one child succeeds on Lua 5.4 and Luau. RecursionGuard removes each table pointer on drop before visiting the sibling."}
{"item":"Public wrapper types lack Debug","loc":"src/chunk.rs:137","sources":["P0094","P0095","P0096","P0097","P0098","P0099","P0100","P0240","P0241","P0242","P0243"],"reports":"AD","status":"not-defect","severity":null,"noise_class":"skill-requested-hygiene","note":"Advisory Clippy reproduces 16 sites, including hidden helpers; source confirms exported Chunk, WeakLua, VmState and iterators lack Debug. This is optional public-API style, not a violated contract."}
{"item":"Unsafe operations lack local invariant comments","loc":"src/userdata/ref.rs:72","sources":["P0101","P0102","P0103","P0104","P0105","P0106","P0107","P0244","P0246","P0247","P0248"],"reports":"AD","status":"not-defect","severity":null,"noise_class":"skill-requested-hygiene","note":"Advisory Clippy reproduces 180 undocumented_unsafe_blocks diagnostics; inspected transmute sites lack local rationale. This is comment/maintainability housekeeping; no runtime defect is claimed or established."}
{"item":"Failed AnyUserData::take allegedly destroys borrowed data","loc":"src/userdata.rs:696","sources":["P0116"],"reports":"B","status":"refuted","severity":null,"noise_class":null,"note":"Borrow-conflicting take returns UserDataBorrowMutError, then borrowing and taking the original 42 succeeds after release. Source checks has_exclusive_access before calling take_userdata; Lua 5.4 and Luau controls pass."}
{"item":"Userdata equality ignores metamethods across different metatables","loc":"src/userdata.rs:955","sources":["P0122"],"reports":"B","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"Two userdata types with the first defining true __eq compare true in Lua 5.4 but false through Value::equals. The early metatable-inequality return contradicts the documented first/second lookup."}
{"item":"Metatable iteration converts restricted values before filtering","loc":"src/userdata.rs:1039","sources":["P0123"],"reports":"B","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"For empty userdata, visible Value entries are all strings, but pairs::<String>() errors converting a hidden boolean/function on Lua 5.4/Luau. TablePairs converts V before restricted keys are skipped."}
{"item":"Narrow integer stack conversion allegedly wraps values","loc":"src/conversion.rs:864","sources":["P0128"],"reports":"B","status":"refuted","severity":null,"noise_class":null,"note":"Evaluating 256 and -1 as u8 returns FromLuaConversionError; 255 succeeds on Lua 5.4 and Luau. The fast path uses num_traits::cast and explicitly rejects out-of-range results."}
{"item":"Invalid table keys abort instead of returning errors","loc":"src/table.rs:258","sources":["P0140","P0157","P0162","P0163","P0164","P0165","P0166","P0167","P0259"],"reports":"CD","status":"ran","severity":"high","noise_class":null,"note":"Separate Lua 5.4 tests for nil/NaN through set/raw_set and nil through create_table_from each terminate with SIGABRT. An 8 MiB limit control returns errors. Unprotected lua_rawset is also at state/raw.rs:575."}
{"item":"Mixed integer/float equality loses integer precision","loc":"src/value.rs:617","sources":["P0146"],"reports":"C","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"Integer(9007199254740993) compares equal to Number(9007199254740992.0) through PartialEq and equals; Lua 5.4 returns false. Casting the integer to f64 erases the difference."}
{"item":"Fixed Serde tuples reject trailing unsupported values despite skipping","loc":"src/serde/de.rs:312","sources":["P0147"],"reports":"C","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"With deny_unsupported_types(false), {1,2,function() end} converts to Vec [1,2] but fails conversion to (i32,i32) with invalid length 3, on Lua 5.4 and Luau. Final validation bypasses skip logic."}
{"item":"Removing a thread hook retains its callback capture","loc":"src/state.rs:624","sources":["P0148","P0219","P0220","P0221","P0222","P0223","P0224"],"reports":"CD","status":"ran","severity":"low","noise_class":null,"note":"Both main-thread and coroutine removal tests leave a captured Arc at strong count 2 after two collections. remove_hook only disables lua_sethook; it leaves the callback registry entry installed."}
{"item":"Boolean closing errors are inverted during thread reset","loc":"src/util/mod.rs:251","sources":["P0150"],"reports":"C","status":"ran","severity":"low","noise_class":null,"note":"Resetting a yielded Lua 5.4 thread whose pending __close calls error(true) returns runtime error: false. The utility tests lua_toboolean != 1 instead of != 0."}
{"item":"Luau vector Serde accepts a tuple with too few components","loc":"src/serde/de.rs:300","sources":["P0200","P0201","P0202","P0203","P0204","P0205"],"reports":"D","status":"ran","severity":"medium","noise_class":null,"note":"A three-component vector succeeds as (f32,f32), while an equivalent table rejects the target and a three-element tuple succeeds. The vector branch never checks remaining components after the visitor."}
{"item":"Replacing a nil registry key allegedly leaves nil","loc":"src/state.rs:1915","sources":["P0245"],"reports":"D","status":"refuted","severity":null,"noise_class":null,"note":"Creating a nil RegistryKey, replacing it with alpha and reading String returns alpha on Lua 5.4 and Luau. The LUA_REFNIL branch creates a new registry key and updates the id."}
